# Verify (VerifyTests/Verify) snapshot files must always use LF line endings, regardless of the
# checking-out machine's core.autocrlf setting -- Verify's own runtime check
# (VerifiedLineEndingException) rejects a verified file containing a carriage return. Without this,
# a Windows CI runner (or any machine with core.autocrlf=true) reintroduces CRLF into the working
# tree on every fresh checkout even though the committed blob itself is LF, since git re-applies its
# line-ending filter on checkout independently of what was normalized at commit time. See
# https://github.com/VerifyTests/Verify#line-ending-autocrlf and the "gitattributes" section of the
# same readme for the exact entries below.
*.verified.txt text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.verified.xml text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.verified.json text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.verified.bin binary
